{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/52048-is-was-the-aberrant-war-unavoidable","id":52048,"title":"Is/Was the Aberrant War unavoidable?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-17T18:45:16-08:00","id":52048,"title":"Is/Was the Aberrant War unavoidable?","content":"Realistically, I kinda think so. Maybe that's even a good thing? Honestly, even with organizations doing all they could to keep regular humans in power, with so many MegaSocial and MegaMental Novas, how long would it have been before they effectively ran the world? A generation or two, at most, I think...Then again, if it weren't for Taint, maybe the world would have been a better place for it? <br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T01:31:43-08:00","id":52221,"title":"","content":"I'd say that some kind of nova-human conflict was unavoidable, but the books say nothing of its nature, scope or scale. Other than the Teragen and a few very small nova organizations, there isn't a 'nova nation' to point an army at. What happens if a nova said &quot;I surrender?&quot; And if it weren't for the Chinese ultimatum, what would of happened if the novas had won the war? <br /> <br /> &quot;Okay, we're at war with the novas. 1st platoon gets sent to Hollywood to round up the ones working there as porn stars.&quot;<br /> <br /> ...?<br /> <br /> Did the war have any real objectives, or was the UN just grasping for a way to deal with the growing number of tainted novas?<br /> <br /> I really think it was just that - nobody knew how to handle things, so someone just threw up their hands (probably at prodding from Proteus) and said 'let's have a war!' And everyone agreed, because they at least knew what a war was, even if they didn't know what the war was supposed to accomplish.<br /> <br /> (Beyond stopping novas from tainting their precious bodily fluids)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-18T10:02:49-08:00","id":52500,"title":"","content":"Nope, but it was certainly likely.<br /> <br /> Conceivably, there were three ways to avoid the Abberant War that I can think of.<br /> <br /> 1) If Project Utopia had successfully solved the Taint problem, or at least found a way to make it manageable, novas flipping out the way that they did could have been a much smaller-scale, more controllable situation (especially with non-Tainted novas on hand to limit damages and prevent people from flipping out). This is demonstrably possible, as shown by the nova world in Trinity. This would, however, have required keeping both normals and novas calm about the whole thing, which would have been difficult (especially with the Teragen around).<br /> <br /> 2) If Project Utopia had convinced some novas that Taint was a problem, they could have triggered a Nova War, which wouldn't have been substantially less devastating because it would have had novas on both sides, but would have at least meant that some of the insane powerhouses were still on their side. A Teragen VS Project Utopia war was totally possible, except that Utopia botched the Taint issue.<br /> <br /> 3) If Proteus had gotten more funding, they could have gone full-murder earlier on, when the issue was still containable, and instigated a nova war of their own by creating and inspiring factional conflict between weaker novas and then assassinating everyone. There was, IIRC, some evidence that they were starting on this in Africa and Kashmir. If they had just a couple of skilled novas who believed it was necessary, they could have instituted a full-on purge that would likely have prevented the Abberant War entirely, at the cost of thousands of innocent nova lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Remember - popcorn can feel pain.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1195-frivyeti","name":"FrivYeti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T06:48:28-08:00","id":59753,"title":"","content":"&quot;Nearly all men can stand adversity, but if you want to test a man's character, give him power.&quot; So, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T11:02:57-08:00","id":59961,"title":"","content":"Just picked this line of games up at a used bookstore (and it was cheap), so not some old hand at this and what your getting amounts to 40 minute quick read, so feel free to disregard.<br /> <br /> The Aberrant War was probably unavoidable, but it didn't have to go down the way it did. So long as one group saw themselves as above the laws of everyone else, it was going to happen. As long as other groups did shadowy things to try and contain large groups of potential threats that hadn't acually done anything wrong, it was going to happen. The taint certainly didn't help, though that would have been manageable if it was the only factor involved. If there were no forced sterilizations, shadowy attempts to contain the Novas, or any other the nonsense that people point to as causes the war, it still would have happened.<br /> <br /> The novas for all their advanced abilities still strike me as fundamentally human with the same core psychological predispositions, and the best predictor of future behavior is past behavior. A quick read of human history pretty much states that some kind of war would have happened eventually, even if it didn't happen the way the books hint at it happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: Unless stated otherwise, all examples I give are completely random and almost assuredly pulled from my nethers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1575-dairugger","name":"Dairugger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1575_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T02:30:09-08:00","id":60592,"title":"","content":"The only unavoidable element was against humanity. I think that if the novas had managed to be manipulated properly by the various groups, then they could have imploded upon themselves. The damage would have been catastrophic in the early stages of the &quot;Nova Civil War&quot; but then the casualties would have been piling up and the damage would have been less and less until all the big guns would either be dead or else they would have been weakened enough for any one of a group of humans to take them down once and for all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T08:43:13-08:00","id":60804,"title":"","content":"Overall, it WAS a Nova Civil War. Humanity did have Nova powerhouses &quot;on its side&quot;. The problem was the fact that the damage escalated so quickly. When you have beings who can create catastrophes with barely a thought, you need a different solution to your war. Hence, the Ultimatum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1006-widdershawns","name":"widdershawns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T19:43:35-08:00","id":63249,"title":"","content":"My whole issue is that the Nova War didn't make sense. I mean..Let's say 1 nova. Just 1 had plank scaling, or Mind Blank, or Quantum Inferno. They could literally annihilate humanity (and any lesser nova defenders with a thought. Or Universe creation? &quot;Oh, the humans here hate me? I'm gonna go over here where the humans love me, peace&quot; It just..I dunno didn't make any sense for humanity to have survived in anything even resembling it's state in Trinity. earth should have been a barren wasteland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/238-hammerofheaven","name":"HammerofHeaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar238_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T21:48:39-08:00","id":63289,"title":"","content":"The War was inevitable I think. The core of Aberrant is that &quot;power corrupts&quot;.. and as Novas continued to grow in power the less &quot;humanity&quot; they would retain.<br /> <br /> Could it of been postponed? For a time sure, but eventually something would of kicked it off.<br /> <br /> My question has always been.. why were there no new eruptions after the Exodus?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2164-mistershifter","name":"MisterShifter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T22:18:48-08:00","id":63297,"title":"","content":"They kinda explain it in the Aberrant players guide. Apparently DiV Mal left, so his changes to human genetics to make Novas possible reverted, and went more toward Psions, so eruptions slowed down/stopped, while it was easier to make Psions. (that's the drift of it) <br /> <br /> APG: 56-60-something. should have the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/238-hammerofheaven","name":"HammerofHeaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar238_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T23:15:35-08:00","id":63319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HammerofHeaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/52048-is-was-the-aberrant-war-unavoidable?p=63297#post63297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They kinda explain it in the Aberrant players guide. Apparently DiV Mal left, so his changes to human genetics to make Novas possible reverted, and went more toward Psions, so eruptions slowed down/stopped, while it was easier to make Psions. (that's the drift of it)<br /> <br /> APG: 56-60-something. should have the answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I read Doctor Primoris (Divis Mal) did not make any changes to human genetics, rather he purposely set an imbalance in the Telluric Energy device hidden aboard Galatea so it would produce a burst that was skewed heavily towards quantum instead of the more balanced one that was planned. It resulted in the incredibly overpowered Novas being produced and only a little nudge in the other types. Since it is exposure to quantum that triggers eruption in those that are potential Novas, after they left there were no active Novas leaking quantum around to trigger more Novas and those that do get triggered are usually triggered by tainted quantum left behind so most erupt into aberrants instead of Novas.<br /> <br /> Psions are actually artificially produced from potentials by a genetic process amplifying their psionic abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T06:38:12-08:00","id":63411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BC001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/52048-is-was-the-aberrant-war-unavoidable?p=63319#post63319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psions are actually artificially produced from potentials by a genetic process amplifying their psionic abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember correctly, that was just the party line. What they were actually doing is neutering your ability with anything other then your primary psionic path. (hence the ability to only buy the first dot of anything else.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T06:50:48-08:00","id":63413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HammerofHeaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/52048-is-was-the-aberrant-war-unavoidable?p=63249#post63249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My whole issue is that the Nova War didn't make sense. I mean..Let's say 1 nova. Just 1 had plank scaling, or Mind Blank, or Quantum Inferno. They could literally annihilate humanity (and any lesser nova defenders with a thought. Or Universe creation? &quot;Oh, the humans here hate me? I'm gonna go over here where the humans love me, peace&quot; It just..I dunno didn't make any sense for humanity to have survived in anything even resembling it's state in Trinity. earth should have been a barren wasteland.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most writers and players are human, and for most humans anything that wipes the species out, even if a transformed version of it will remain is frightening beyond belief and not a happy ending regardless of how that ending came to be. So even in the event that we all evolve into something not really human peacefully and the universe is a much better place for it, the fact that humanity as we understand it is GONE means it is, at best, a bittersweet ending in most people's eyes. So that's why it happened the way it did in the game.<br /> <br /> So, yes, I'm actually agreeing that in-universe your comments makes 100% sense to me and I agree with you. In real life, I just accept it as human-centrist thoughts not allowing for the complete wipe out of the species.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: Unless stated otherwise, all examples I give are completely random and almost assuredly pulled from my nethers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1575-dairugger","name":"Dairugger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1575_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T09:16:53-08:00","id":63462,"title":"","content":"I'm of the opinion that outright war could have been avoided, but the Teragen and Project Proteus would have both need to have been delt with first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T01:51:25-08:00","id":64684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HammerofHeaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/52048-is-was-the-aberrant-war-unavoidable?p=63249#post63249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My whole issue is that the Nova War didn't make sense. I mean..Let's say 1 nova. Just 1 had plank scaling, or Mind Blank, or Quantum Inferno. They could literally annihilate humanity (and any lesser nova defenders with a thought. Or Universe creation? &quot;Oh, the humans here hate me? I'm gonna go over here where the humans love me, peace&quot; It just..I dunno didn't make any sense for humanity to have survived in anything even resembling it's state in Trinity. earth should have been a barren wasteland.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're assuming the Aberrant Player's Guide presents everything that the Novas/Aberrants were capable of by the end of the war. Now, we have examples of Level 5 powers being put to use here and there (Mal kickstarting the massive quantum awakening, for instance), but there's no evidence that any single Nova was capable of destroying the planet before the Ultimatum. Maybe one or more of the Novas could have wiped out humanity, but doing so without also destroying the planet (or rendering it completely uninhabitable, even by Nova standards) might have taken too long and too much effort to be worthwhile. Quantum Inferno's a powerful attack, sure, but it's not really something you want to spend time and energy using on individual targets smaller than a planet unless you're in deep space or something. But even then, the power to destroy the world isn't the same as the desire no matter how Tainted you are. <br /> <br /> It's a pretty safe bet that when the Ultimatum was presented, the crash of the OpNet was the closest any Novas had come to openly doing something that could end civilization. (And even then, they did it by accident.) Of course, I wouldn't be surprised if there are a couple of Novas who called their bluff and said &quot;I'll survive the destruction of the planet. Bring it.&quot; only to be dealt with quietly by friendlier Novas (and subsequently scrubbed from history).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T15:43:13-08:00","id":68123,"title":"","content":"To avoid the Aberrant War:<br /> <br /> Step 1: DELETE PROTEUS. This will simultaneously delete the Aberrant faction as they have nothing to react against.<br /> <br /> Step 2: BLACKLIST any nova attempting to join the Teragen pantheon other than Orzaiz, Fong, Scripture, Mathematician, Bounty, and Apothecary, PERIOD. Watch in awe as it transforms into a scientific think-tank.<br /> <br /> Step 3: Unchain the UN from Utopia, MAKE them stand on their own. Utopia can be the nonprofit organization it pretends to be instead of a shadow-power.<br /> <br /> Step 4: Divide the Directive into like-minded intel agencies that have jurisdiction ONLY in their own nations, then point them at the megasyndicate and everything like it.<br /> <br /> Step 5: Focus MORE attention on the Daedalus League and their extrasolar explorations so mankind's collective mind is distracted by SPACE.<br /> <br /> Step 6: Profit!<br /> <br /> Backup plan 5a: Stumble across the Chromatics and trigger interstellar war. All human species and ethnicities are now united in defending against the aliens (literally the only way that works...EVER).<br /> <br /> Backup plan 5b: Flood the world with data on the two other species humans evolve into (psiads and whatever paramorphs are), the resulting confusion staves off war for decades till the frogs invade. See backup plan 5a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":765,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","user":"Darksol-aeternium","date":". 02-08-2014, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T16:58:21-08:00","id":68149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/52048-is-was-the-aberrant-war-unavoidable?p=68123#post68123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Backup plan 5b: Flood the world with data on the two other species humans evolve into (psiads and whatever paramorphs are), the resulting confusion staves off war for decades till the frogs invade. See backup plan 5a.</div> </div> </div> </div>Homo sapiens sapiens have two offshoots: Homo sapiens novus and Homo sapiens mentis. Paramorphs are not a new subspecies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T19:28:22-08:00","id":68765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/52048-is-was-the-aberrant-war-unavoidable?p=68123#post68123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To avoid the Aberrant War:<br /> <br /> Step 1: DELETE PROTEUS. This will simultaneously delete the Aberrant faction as they have nothing to react against.<br /> <br /> Step 2: BLACKLIST any nova attempting to join the Teragen pantheon other than Orzaiz, Fong, Scripture, Mathematician, Bounty, and Apothecary, PERIOD. Watch in awe as it transforms into a scientific think-tank.<br /> <br /> Step 3: Unchain the UN from Utopia, MAKE them stand on their own. Utopia can be the nonprofit organization it pretends to be instead of a shadow-power.<br /> <br /> Step 4: Divide the Directive into like-minded intel agencies that have jurisdiction ONLY in their own nations, then point them at the megasyndicate and everything like it.<br /> <br /> Step 5: Focus MORE attention on the Daedalus League and their extrasolar explorations so mankind's collective mind is distracted by SPACE.<br /> <br /> Step 6: Profit!<br /> <br /> Backup plan 5a: Stumble across the Chromatics and trigger interstellar war. All human species and ethnicities are now united in defending against the aliens (literally the only way that works...EVER).<br /> <br /> Backup plan 5b: Flood the world with data on the two other species humans evolve into (psiads and whatever paramorphs are), the resulting confusion staves off war for decades till the frogs invade. See backup plan 5a.</div> </div> </div> </div>Proteus would have to have been retroactively deleted somehow, by 2008 when the original \u201cgame now\u201d was they had already done severe irreversible damage to the Nova situation. Squashing it even right away as far as the game start time goes might calm things slightly but most likely not enough. The 21st century Aberrant faction had a mostly undeserved bad reputation (so much so that all Novas are later referred to by that name) but they really were not a big player in starting the war itself from what I have read.<br /> <br /> The Chromatics would not be any kind of threat; not only were they steamrollered easily by the 22nd century Novas once they were brought in, they were a peaceful primitive people until the Psion creatures (I forget their name offhand) modified and armed them as a weapon in their overcomplicated plan to stop the threat of the Aberrants loose in the galaxy. Since the war and its exile of the Novas at the end of it would not have happened yet the Psion energy creatures would not have been looking for proxy weapons against them and so a Chromatic invasion in the 21st century could not happen. Of course if the original Novas started exploring space more it may trigger a similar reaction at an earlier time and start the ball rolling for a Chromatic invasion sooner than it was in the modules.<br /> <br /> Of course that does not prevent a campaign where the players either know or at least suspect the war is coming and try to prevent it from happening (I ran a campaign that revolved around an effort like that for instance).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","user":"BC001","date":". 02-09-2014, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T20:21:22-08:00","id":68776,"title":"","content":"It is assumed that the plan must be implemented as of 1998 at the very latest, though you are right I probably should have specified.<br /> <br /> Yes, the Chromatics will get steamrolled, but that's not the point. The very fact of a potential threat from space creates a lingering paranoia in the human mind that will have them watching the stars like hawks and stockpiling any weapon they can find. If one alien race has beef with Earth others might, and that's all the flimsy justification the human mind needs to prep for war. The Doyen (the psi race you were talking about) would just find a new patsy to use against Earth if the Chromatics fail, so all the wartime buildup would be justified. Hell, additional funding would go towards colonization so we could setup numerous early warning systems (and military garrisons) all through the solar system.<br /> <br /> Trinity-era Earth is just as factionalized and divided as Earth has ever been, if AEON really want's to unify mankind, they need to sell the threat from outside (i.e. SPACE).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T13:39:57-08:00","id":74527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/52048-is-was-the-aberrant-war-unavoidable?p=68123#post68123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To avoid the Aberrant War:<br /> <br /> Step 1: DELETE PROTEUS. This will simultaneously delete the Aberrant faction as they have nothing to react against.<br /> <br /> Step 2: BLACKLIST any nova attempting to join the Teragen pantheon other than Orzaiz, Fong, Scripture, Mathematician, Bounty, and Apothecary, PERIOD. Watch in awe as it transforms into a scientific think-tank.<br /> <br /> Step 3: Unchain the UN from Utopia, MAKE them stand on their own. Utopia can be the nonprofit organization it pretends to be instead of a shadow-power.<br /> <br /> Step 4: Divide the Directive into like-minded intel agencies that have jurisdiction ONLY in their own nations, then point them at the megasyndicate and everything like it.<br /> <br /> Step 5: Focus MORE attention on the Daedalus League and their extrasolar explorations so mankind's collective mind is distracted by SPACE.<br /> <br /> Step 6: Profit!<br /> <br /> Backup plan 5a: Stumble across the Chromatics and trigger interstellar war. All human species and ethnicities are now united in defending against the aliens (literally the only way that works...EVER).<br /> <br /> Backup plan 5b: Flood the world with data on the two other species humans evolve into (psiads and whatever paramorphs are), the resulting confusion staves off war for decades till the frogs invade. See backup plan 5a.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you considered that the Aberrant War as it played out was the least horrible outcome?<br /> <br /> Step 1: Something else will replace Proteus. There's always going to be &quot;need&quot; for the poison dagger held by the iron fist in the velvet glove.<br /> <br /> Step 2: Good luck Blacklisting Divis Mal from his own organization, but whatever. Fine, they're blacklisted. So, they'll form their own, more violent organizations without cooler heads to reign them in.<br /> <br /> Step 3: So we'll have something like a cross between the Red Cross and Charles Xavier's School for the Gifted. And meanwhile the individual members of the UN will have a worldwide Nova arms race because there will be no UN-backed Utopia to stop them.<br /> <br /> Step 4: Because turf wars and information hoarding will be extremely helpful in dealing a worldwide situation.<br /> <br /> Step 5: Yes, let's get the Novas thinking about Space. Who knows, when hostilities do flare up, they might well decided to target humanity's colonies first and make the Chinese Ultimatum meaningless.<br /> <br /> Step 6: Or ANNIHILATION!<br /> <br /> 5a: The reason that the Chromatics were persuaded by the Doyen to go after humanity was that human Aberrants attacked them first.<br /> <br /> 5b: Cool. We can spread the word about undetectable mentalists and other beings with Nova-like abilities. A massive shot of paranoia is just what the world needs.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't mean to come off harsh, even if that's how I seem above. If you want a silver bullet for the Aberrant War, stop Galatea explosion. Prevent novas and there won't be a nova war. Of course, it's easily possible that the appearance of novas prevented some horrible fate from destroying humanity. Who knows?<br /> <br /> Which is the point. No one really knows. Awful as it was, humanity survived the Aberrant War and even thrived in the aftermath. Sure things are tough in 2120+ but there's plenty of hope as well. It's been a long time ago, but I recall posting an adventure outline on the old White Wolf board that dealt with the AEON group of the previous published adventures going on a diplomatic voyage to Eden to help negotiate an alliance with them against the Coalition. Bruce Baugh commented that this idea was very close to where Trinity would have gone next. The arc of the future bends toward hope. Studying the past is good, Trying to changing is either impossible or a really, really bad idea. Aeon is a continuum. Disrupt one part of that continuum and you're likely to get something much different and much worse than what you wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T18:48:57-08:00","id":74713,"title":"","content":"The galatea explosion was nothing but a red herring, an excuse to camouflage Divis Mal's one-sided telluric energy incident. If you really want to stop everything before it starts KILL MAX MERCER BEFORE HE STARTS HOPPING THROUGH TIME. Like you just said, messing with time is usually a bad idea, so why should he get away with it?<br /> <br /> Letting AEON and all it's affiliates and subdivisions get away with genocide, and then allowing them a few hundred years for them to come to their senses, sounds like letting the nazis off with a warning if they say &quot;sorry, we messed up!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-19T11:04:14-08:00","id":75076,"title":"","content":"There's no thing such as &quot;avoiding war&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T12:50:39-08:00","id":75817,"title":"","content":"<br /> So a Mega-Wits Test Difficulty +5, should allow you to &quot;Ambush War&quot;, follow that up with a MEga-Appearance Test Difficulty +5, to Seduce Peace. Then finish it off, with a Mega Charisma Test Difficulty +5 of Charm Nation. This should allow you to to &quot;Dodge War&quot;... assuming we were all talking about the Mega-Social combat system...&lt;JK&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1336-gideon","name":"Gideon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1336_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T05:58:53-08:00","id":76219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/52048-is-was-the-aberrant-war-unavoidable?p=74713#post74713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The galatea explosion was nothing but a red herring, an excuse to camouflage Divis Mal's one-sided telluric energy incident. If you really want to stop everything before it starts KILL MAX MERCER BEFORE HE STARTS HOPPING THROUGH TIME. Like you just said, messing with time is usually a bad idea, so why should he get away with it?<br /> <br /> Letting AEON and all it's affiliates and subdivisions get away with genocide, and then allowing them a few hundred years for them to come to their senses, sounds like letting the nazis off with a warning if they say &quot;sorry, we messed up!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not quite sure where killing Max or getting rid of the Aeon society factors in. First off, Max started hopping through time during the original Hammersmith explosion. The same one that empowered Michael Donighal (aka Doctor Primoris, aka Divis Mal) in the first place. Second, even if you could stop that, there actually isn't a whole lot of evidence of Max actually doing that much time travel-related meddling. The Aeon Society is not an organization of murderers or wicked schemers undermining society with steepled fingers and cackling grins in dark, smoky rooms. Proteus was a perversion of the Aeon Society's philosophies and resources and it got way out of control. And while I'm not saying it all magically balances out, it's largely due to Aeon's existence that there was an infrastructure geared towards encouraging novas to improve the world in the first place (or at keeping them from destroying the world by accident in the first couple of years). In my personal opinion the world (as presented in the setting) is better with the Aeon Society than without it.<br /> <br /> Also, the Galatea Explosion wasn't any sort of camouflage. A red herring of sorts, sure, but an unintentional one. It was a side-effect of Divis Mal's attempt to elevate humanity. (It was said back when the game line was still originally running that the Galatea Explosion was in fact the first major nova eruption after Divis Mal did his thing.) And again, killing Max Mercer wouldn't prevent the appearance of the novas. (I'd have to dig out my books and check the timeline, but I think it was the Aeon Society that stopped Divis Mal from actually trying to conquer the world back in the 40's)<br /> <br /> If there's really is a single &quot;Go back in time and kill this guy and it's all better&quot; lynchpin, it's Hammersmith more than anyone else. The only way to really stop a war between any metahuman faction and anyone else (whether it's another faction or the rest of humanity) is to take the superpowers out of the equation.<br /> <br /> The Nazi comparison, not even taking Godwin's Law into account, doesn't really hold water here. Declaring all of the Aeon Society to be responsible for the Aberrant War (many aspects of which were outside even Proteus' control) is like declaring <i>all</i> Germans -- including citizens and the resistance groups -- responsible for the Holocaust as well as the Nazis. Aeon as a whole is not responsible for Proteus' manipulations, and there's evidence in the books that there are a lot of individuals in the Society who would not have approved of Proteus' actions.<br /> <br /> Finally, given the damage that was done to the world in the Aberrant War, I don't think it's fair to say that anyone 'got away' with anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T08:25:43-08:00","id":77083,"title":"","content":"For a bit in the mid 2000s I was simultaneously in two different Aberrant games, which was a little odd to say the least. There was substantial player overlap but different STs who had very different takes on how things ran. I had to leave before both games finished, sadly. <br /> <br /> In one the Aberrant War was something one of the factions of novas was trying to start early, as they could see the future and feared it greatly! I was playing a psiad who worked for the AEon Society, had precog, Meta-Wits, and similar kinds of traits, including the ability to stealth against Novas. Things were definitely on an ugly trajectory. For instance, a nova erupting in Kampala, Uganda, went off with the force of a small nuke. Said nova was later deep-sixed by Proteus. In this chronicle Divis Mal wasn't Doctor Primorus. The latter was an old mad scientist from the Adventure! days. We also ran into Danger Ace, who was old. <br /> <br /> The other one was quite different. That had old Novas hiding out in space by Alpha Centauri. My character in that game was a flyer who bought up some heavy duty transportation powers, including the portal one. (The character's basis was as a Farsi who was slowly becoming a Zoroastrian angel, or deva, depending on how things played.) I was the first Nova in space, the first Nova to go to Alpha Centauri, etc. (At least as far as anyone knew....) After I left the game my character ended up becoming the equivalent of the Silver Surfer as the herald for the old novas. <br /> <br /> Regardless, I have to say that humanity's historical record on stopping wars is pretty darn poor. Add in Novas and a general cult of Celebrity and I just don't buy it. The Aberrant War probably came out about as well as things possibly could!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2173-jvv","name":"JVV","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}